```java
interface Engine {
    void start();
}

final class PetrolEngine implements Engine {
    public void start() { System.out.println("petrol"); }
}

final class Car {
    private final Engine engine;

    Car(Engine engine) {
        this.engine = engine;
    }

    void start() {
        engine.start();
    }
}

Car car = new Car(new PetrolEngine());
```

`Car` uses composition and its engine is fixed after construction. A different `Car` can receive another `Engine`; this object does not magically swap collaborators at runtime.

```java
interface Notifier {
    void send(String message);
}

final class OrderService {
    private final Notifier notifier;

    OrderService(Notifier notifier) {
        this.notifier = notifier;
    }

    void placeOrder() {
        // Save the order, then notify the customer.
        notifier.send("Order placed");
    }
}

OrderService service = new OrderService(new EmailNotifier());
```

The collaborator is selected when `OrderService` is created. Production can provide `EmailNotifier`, while a focused test can provide a fake. This is a useful seam, not a promise that the same service object can hot-swap its notifier later.

```java
class Bag {
    protected final List<String> values = new ArrayList<>();

    public void add(String value) { values.add(value); }

    // Version 1: bulk operation writes directly.
    public void addAll(List<String> input) { values.addAll(input); }
}

class CountingBag extends Bag {
    private int added;

    @Override public void add(String value) {
        added++;
        super.add(value);
    }

    @Override public void addAll(List<String> input) {
        added += input.size();
        super.addAll(input);
    }
}
```

If `Bag.addAll` is later refactored to `for (String value : input) add(value);`, normal `Bag` results are unchanged, but `CountingBag.addAll` counts once in its own override and again through the overridable `add` calls.

```java
abstract class Shape {
    abstract double area();

    String describe() {
        return "area=" + area();
    }
}

final class Circle extends Shape {
    private final double radius;

    Circle(double radius) {
        if (radius < 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException("radius");
        this.radius = radius;
    }

    @Override double area() {
        return Math.PI * radius * radius;
    }
}

void printArea(Shape shape) {
    System.out.println(shape.describe());
}

printArea(new Circle(2));
```

This inheritance is useful because callers need the `Shape` contract and `Circle` preserves its rules. The class names alone do not prove the design; the contract does.

// Component interface
public interface DataSource {
    String readData();
}

// Concrete component
public class FileDataSource implements DataSource {
    private final String filename;

    public FileDataSource(String filename) { this.filename = filename; }

    @Override
    public String readData() {
        return "[file content from " + filename + "]";
    }
}

// Base decorator holds wrapped component
public abstract class DataSourceDecorator implements DataSource {
    protected final DataSource wrappee; // composition

    protected DataSourceDecorator(DataSource source) {
        this.wrappee = source;
    }

    @Override
    public String readData() {
        return wrappee.readData(); // delegates to wrapped
    }
}

// Concrete decorator adds encryption
public class EncryptionDecorator extends DataSourceDecorator {
    public EncryptionDecorator(DataSource source) { super(source); }

    @Override
    public String readData() {
        var data = super.readData(); // delegate first
        return "[encrypted: " + data + "]"; // add behavior after
    }
}

// Concrete decorator adds compression
public class CompressionDecorator extends DataSourceDecorator {
    public CompressionDecorator(DataSource source) { super(source); }

    @Override
    public String readData() {
        var data = super.readData();
        return "[compressed: " + data + "]"; // add behavior after
    }
}

// Compose at runtime - no subclass explosion
DataSource source = new CompressionDecorator(
                        new EncryptionDecorator(
                            new FileDataSource("data.txt")));
String result = source.readData();
// result: "[compressed: [encrypted: [file content from data.txt]]]"
